  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development to which this permission relates must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of the decision notice.\n\nReason: To comply with the provisions of S.51 of the Planning & Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the approved plans, as set out in the attached schedule which forms part of this notice.\n\nReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.",
    "Prior to the commencement of above ground works full details of all external finishing materials to be used in the development shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority.\n\nThe development shall be constructed in accordance with the approved details.\n\nReason: To secure a satisfactory appearance in accordance with the development plan policies.",
    "Prior to the commencement of above ground works full details of a landscaping strategy shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority.\n\nThese details shall include: existing planting to be retained; trees, shrubs and grass to be planted; the treatment of any hard surfaced areas; and, the means of enclosure of any unbuilt land on the site.\n\nThe site shall be landscaped in accordance with the approved details in the first planting season after completion or occupation of the development, whichever is the sooner. Any trees or shrubs which die, becomes severely damaged or diseased within five years of planting shall be replaced with new planting in accordance with the approved details. \n\nReason: To ensure a satisfactory appearance in accordance with DMD 81 of the Enfield Development Management Document 2014.",
    "Prior to the commencement of above ground works details demonstrating how the drainage of surface water from any hardstanding in the development will be prevented from discharging on to the public highway shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority.\n\nThe surfacing and drainage measures shall be carried out in accordance with the approved details.\n\nReason: To ensure water does not drain towards the highway, adversely impact highway safety and increase the risk of flooding elsewhere.",
    "Prior to first occupation of the development details of the internal consumption of potable water shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The submitted details shall demonstrate reduced water consumption through the use of water efficient fittings, flow restrictions, efficient appliances and water recycling/harvesting systems where feasible and achieve a water consumption rate of less than 105 litres per person per day.\n\nThe development shall be carried out in accordance with the approved details and maintained as such thereafter.\n\nReason: To minimise water consumption in accordance with DMD 58 of the Enfield Development Management Document 2014.",
    "Prior to first occupation of the development full details of two (2) secure and covered cycle parking space shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority.\n\nThe cycle parking shall be installed in accordance with the approved details prior to first occupation of the development and maintained as such thereafter.\n\nReason: To ensure the provision of cycle parking in line with the Council's adopted standards.",
    "Prior to first occupation of the development full details of the refuse and recycling storage facilities shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority.\n\nThe development shall be carried out in accordance with these approved details and maintained as such thereafter.\n\nReason: In the interests of maintaining the quality of the street scene in accordance with DMD 8 of the Enfield Development Management Document 2014.",
    "Notwithstanding the provisions of Classes A, B, D and E of Part 1 of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 2015, or any amending or superseding Order, no buildings or extensions to buildings shall be erected without the formal written consent of the Local Planning Authority.\n\nReason: To maintain a satisfactory appearance and adequate private amenity space for future occupiers."
  ],
